{"type": "message", "message": "**Minimalist means keeping what earns its place—not making your flat empty.** In a small home, it’s about a complete, comfortable setup with less visual clutter.\n\n- **Simple, useful furniture:** comfortable seating, a reachable table, lighting and enough storage—not lots of little pieces.\n- **A restrained palette:** a few related colours and materials. Warm wood and textured fabrics can keep it welcoming rather than stark.\n- **Clear routes:** arrange furniture so doors, windows and everyday destinations are easy to reach.\n- **Mostly closed storage:** give everyday belongings a home without putting everything on display.\n- **A few personal accents:** favourite objects stand out more when they have breathing room.\n\nFor your combined living room and kitchen, I’d aim for distinct sitting and eating areas that share a calm palette, while keeping the route to the balcony clear. That’s a design direction, not a checked layout or an applied change.", "conversationId": "f8959150ac0d4ba5a0592d8447f0d96d"}
